<title>GERMANY: Germany's Stark says EMU formulated to be stable.</title>
<headline>Germany's Stark says EMU formulated to be stable.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German state secretary to the finance ministry Juergen Stark said on Thursday that European economic and monetary union (EMU) had been constructed so that the euro would be a stable currency.</p>
<p>EMU had been formulated with agreements on rules, regulations and obligations &quot;to ensure that the euro currency will be a stable currency,&quot; Stark said.</p>
<p>-- Berlin Newsroom + 49 30 203 9810</p>
</text>
